    "q-130963": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130963",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 5 & 0 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
