    "q-131305": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131305",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th columns.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
